WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:07.060
Game of Thrones Season 8 is the most anticipated
TV release of 2019, and HBO has been super

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:09.370
secretive about the production.

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:14.100
But it looks like some footage has leaked
from the new season, revealing surprising

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:19.040
twists in the future of Jon Snow, Cersei Arya,
and others.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:24.150
In this leaked shot, it looks like Jon is
captured by Dothraki – just like Daenerys

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:25.860
was in Season 6.

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:31.730
Jon is then forced to fight as a gladiator
in what looks like Daznak’s Pit in Meereen.

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:36.390
It is surprising that Jon is here is in the
east instead of fighting white walkers in

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:37.520
Westeros.

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:40.449
But this arc seems important for Jon personally.

00:00:40.449 --> 00:00:46.019
Cause there’s this dream sequence with Jon
and Ned Stark, the man who Jon thinks was

00:00:46.019 --> 00:00:47.019
his father.

00:00:47.019 --> 00:00:52.379
Jon tries to free Ned from chains while the
Mountain swings a sword around with a triangle

00:00:52.379 --> 00:00:53.609
on his head.

00:00:53.609 --> 00:00:58.739
The theme here is that Jon feels trapped in
his responsibilities, when his true passion

00:00:58.739 --> 00:01:04.339
is to train and become the top ranked professional
tennis player in Westeros – as well as a

00:01:04.339 --> 00:01:09.119
three time cover model for Men’s Health
magazine, like Khal Drogo before him.

00:01:09.119 --> 00:01:14.520
So this is a surprising but inspiring conclusion
to Jon’s story.

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:20.439
In Season 7, Queen Cersei plans to hire a
mercenary army to help her win Westeros . And

00:01:20.439 --> 00:01:25.920
in this leaked shot, she gets her army, and
Cersei personally leads them to battle.

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:30.550
But this might go badly for her, cause it
looks like Cersei’s wounded, and even loses

00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:31.890
an eye.

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:33.360
Who does this to her?

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:38.770
Well, Arya Stark wants to kill Cersei, and
here we see Arya wearing crimson and gold

00:01:38.770 --> 00:01:43.990
– maybe she uses her Faceless magic to infiltrate
the Lannisters, joins their army, and tries

00:01:43.990 --> 00:01:45.479
to assassinate Cersei.

00:01:45.479 --> 00:01:51.969
But Cersei won’t go down easy – she upgrades
her ballista to a minigun, and goes all Neo

00:01:51.969 --> 00:01:53.500
on Stark asses.

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:56.450
Luckily, Hodor returns to stop her.

00:01:56.450 --> 00:02:02.119
But Arya flees the war to take up a life of
crime with a strange old man.

00:02:02.119 --> 00:02:07.010
Sansa gets fed up with being the only Stark
who doesn’t have a superpower – like,

00:02:07.010 --> 00:02:12.040
Arya’s a shapeshifting ninja, Bran’s a
psychic, Jon can’t bloody die – so Sansa

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:15.820
decides to learn telekinesis, and the power
of flight.

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:22.170
We see her explode with fire and light, finally
confirming that Sansa is Azor Ahai, the prophesied

00:02:22.170 --> 00:02:24.530
hero who’ll save Westeros.

00:02:24.530 --> 00:02:27.720
This is a dramatic change in Sansa’s destiny.

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:30.150
But she remains loyal to her family.

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:35.920
Because her new tattoo is of a direwolf – representing
her love for House Stark.

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:39.860
Last season, Daenerys embraced her power as
a Targaryen queen.

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:42.730
But she still seems torn in her identity.

00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:47.120
Here she wears white fur with a red scarf
tight round her neck.

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:52.640
The scarf represents Dany’s role as a Targaryen
queen, while the white fur refers to the white

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:56.750
lions-coat Dany wears in the books in her
role as khaleesi.

00:02:56.750 --> 00:03:00.330
So Dany feels torn between her past and her
future.

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:03.070
Her solution is a rejection of both.

00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:07.740
Instead of using mighty Targaryen dragons
as her weapons, Dany decides to just shoot

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:08.740
cunts.

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:14.670
Guns are way easier to manage than dragons,
and this saves HBO money on expensive CGI.

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:18.770
So expect fewer dragons in Season 8.

00:03:18.770 --> 00:03:22.360
Last time we saw Jaime, he left Cersei and
rode north.

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:27.460
But it looks like his breakup with his lifelong
lover really hurts Jaime emotionally.

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:33.530
He ends up changing his look with a handlebar
moustache and some highly symbolic tattoos.

00:03:33.530 --> 00:03:39.220
The name Katherine may refer to Catelyn, who
Jaime swore an oath to in Season 1.

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:44.640
This image of a beheading may refer to Ned
Stark, who Jaime attacked before Ned’s death.

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:49.320
And this cross may refer to the inn at the
crossroads where Catelyn captured Tyrion,

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:51.540
and sparked the Lannister-Stark war.

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:57.330
So these tattoos are a tapestry of Jaime’s
feelings of guilt to the Starks, but it also

00:03:57.330 --> 00:03:59.690
refers to his own family.

00:03:59.690 --> 00:04:05.910
This spiderweb design refers to Jaime great-grandmother
Rohanne of House Webber – look it up nerds.

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:11.450
So Jaime’s tattoos represent the conflicts
that will define him and his moustache in

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:13.590
the season to come.

00:04:13.590 --> 00:04:18.290
In Season 7, Tyrion tried to help his queen
through strategic advice – all of which

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:20.070
failed disastrously.

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:25.630
So it looks like next season, Tyrion tries
to use other skills, like his combat prowess

00:04:25.630 --> 00:04:27.220
and business acumen.

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:33.000
But ultimately, Tyrion does a Radagast and
retires to the woods to become a bearded hermit.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:36.370
Maybe he wasn’t cut out for the game of
thrones after all.

00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:41.450
Karl “Fookin” Tanner and Ellaria Sand
seemed dead, but it now looks like they’re

00:04:41.450 --> 00:04:44.770
alive, running a promising tech startup in
Cardiff.

00:04:44.770 --> 00:04:50.110
Gilly decides to break up with Sam, and moves
to Bristol to shack up with Gendry.

00:04:50.110 --> 00:04:53.780
Sam is so heartbroken that he joins the Faith.

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:59.291
Hot Pie started the series as an amoral bully,
before growing into a slightly more noble

00:04:59.291 --> 00:05:00.291
character.

00:05:00.291 --> 00:05:06.020
But sadly, the leaks show Hot Pie returning
to petty bullying – stealing an ice cream

00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:08.470
cone from a small child.

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:13.630
It turns out that Margaery survived Cersei’s
wildfire last season with only her hair burned

00:05:13.630 --> 00:05:14.630
off.

00:05:14.630 --> 00:05:18.300
She gets a Tyrell tattoo to commemorate her
dead family.

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:21.470
The Hound suffers a tragic head injury.

00:05:21.470 --> 00:05:24.550
Bronn finally gets the retirement he always
wanted.

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:30.670
And Tywin suffers in his own personal hell
for his crimes against Westeros.

00:05:30.670 --> 00:05:33.680
So this looks to be a bold Season 8.

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:40.010
We’re getting surprising twists in major
storylines, and some fresh new character makeovers.

00:05:40.010 --> 00:05:43.000
But it’s a shame that all this footage was
leaked.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:48.310
You’d think that by now, HBO would fix their
online security –Thrones Season 5 was hacked

00:05:48.310 --> 00:05:55.340
in 2015 , then again in 2017 . HBO must be
using insecure passwords or something.

